change.Q1:
(a) Prudent. ai_order(w, id) returns None before any read when either switch is off, and None for the player's nation. It reads legality on the post-lapse view (contract 4.4). It walks the Army ordinals in stored order and, for each, the scopes from widest to narrowest. It returns the first AssertCivilianAuthority that meets all of these conditions:
- it is legal (section 5 rules 1-14, plus the saved-power rule of Q6);
- its OrderPlan.complies is true, i.e. acceptance >= .35;
- D < .25 (C14), government_seats() >= .50 (C13), and political_capital >= AUTHORITY_ORDER_PC + AI_ORDER_RESERVE_PC (Q9).
It returns nothing when no such order exists. The AI never issues an order its own plan says would be refused, so it opens no dispute. ai_response runs at clock::month_end from ai_government, for electoral non-player nations whose record passes pending_lapse. Its only response is Withdraw, a fallback that AI-issued orders cannot reach. It never acts on the player's dispute and draws no RNG.

