implementation_readings.R1_Q2_Q3:
Q3(b) needs the card choice before the order can be considered, so the order is added in ai_stratagems' (None, None) arm and not as the contract's drafted ai_lever branch (11.4). As a result:
- ai_lever and the A1 observer's selected_lever field are unchanged;
- the_ai_takes_each_lever_only_under_its_thresholds must pass unmodified.

implementation_readings.R4_Q9:
AI_ORDER_RESERVE_PC = 68 is the largest political-capital holding that any other AI use needs at the base:
- SuspendConstitution needs pc >= 55 (ai_lever);
- BanParty needs pc >= 60 (ai_lever);
- SecurePillar needs held > 55 (ai_government);
- cards need held >= 55 and cost <= held - 20, and the deck's most expensive card costs 48 (nuclear_programme), so 48 + 20 = 68.
After paying 25 PC, an issuing AI still holds at least 68, so none of these uses is starved. A unit test computes the card term from DECK and asserts the reserve is at least every term.

implementation_readings.R13_stop_rule:
A 'regression' is any of these:
- an original gate that passes at the baseline fails on the candidate;
- A1's count leaves 4..=14;
- either Algeria chronology test fails.
A value that moves inside a passing band is reported with its direction. It is not a rejection trigger.

